---
import GenericPageLayout from '../../layouts/GenericPageLayout.astro';
import styles from '../../styles/academics.module.css';
---

<GenericPageLayout 
  title="Examination Timetable & Guidelines" 
  subtitle="Rules, regulations, and preparations for university exams."
  heroImage="/media/DSC_4804.webp"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics' },
    { label: 'Examinations', href: '/academics/exams' }
  ]}
>
  <div class={styles.contentWrapper}>
    
    <div class={styles.importantBox}>
      <strong>First Semester Examinations, 2024/2025:</strong> The final timetable draft has been uploaded to the student portal. Ensure you have printed your valid examination clearance card before entering the halls.
    </div>

    <h2 class={styles.heading2}>Examination Rules & Regulations</h2>
    <p class={styles.paragraph}>
      The University maintains a zero-tolerance policy towards examination malpractice. To ensure a smooth, fair, and secure examination process, all candidates must strictly observe the following rules:
    </p>

    <ul class={styles.list}>
      <li>Candidates must arrive at the examination venue at least <strong>30 minutes</strong> before the scheduled paper time for biometric verification.</li>
      <li>Students without their official University ID Card and Examination Clearance Form will <strong>NOT</strong> be allowed into the hall.</li>
      <li>Mobile phones, smartwatches, programmable calculators, and any piece of unauthorized blank or written paper are strictly prohibited.</li>
      <li>Silence must be maintained at all times. Communicating with other candidates during an ongoing examination is an offense punishable by expulsion.</li>
      <li>No candidate may leave the hall within the first 45 minutes of the examination, nor in the final 15 minutes of the examination time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={styles.heading2}>Grading System</h2>
    <p class={styles.paragraph}>
      FUAZ operates a 5-point Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) system as prescribed by the National Universities Commission (NUC).
    </p>

    <div class={styles.dataTableWrap}>
      <table class={styles.dataTable}>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Score Range</th>
            <th>Letter Grade</th>
            <th>Grade Point</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class={styles.dateCol}>70% - 100%</td><td>A</td><td>5.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td class={styles.dateCol}>60% - 69%</td><td>B</td><td>4.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td class={styles.dateCol}>50% - 59%</td><td>C</td><td>3.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td class={styles.dateCol}>45% - 49%</td><td>D</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td class={styles.dateCol}>0% - 44%</td><td>F</td><td>0.00</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class={styles.paragraph}>
      If you experience any conflicts or missing courses in your timetable, immediately consult your departmental course adviser or the exams and records office.
    </p>

  </div>
</GenericPageLayout>
